<h3>What's here?</h3>
<h4><i>small things that make the web interesting</i></h4>

<div class="grid grid-3 no-border">

    <div class="card">
        <b>Websites</b><br>
        Personal websites, blogs, digital gardens,
        portfolios, and independent spaces.
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <b>RSS</b><br>
        Follow websites and blogs directly through
        feeds instead of relying on algorithms.
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <b>Open Source</b><br>
        Discover software, libraries, tools, and projects
        whose source code is open to everyone.
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <b>Decentralization</b><br>
        Explore distributed networks, protocols,
        peer-to-peer systems, and alternative infrastructure.
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <b>DeGoogle</b><br>
        Learn about privacy-friendly tools and ways
        to reduce dependence on centralized platforms.
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <b>Privacy</b><br>
        Discuss privacy, encryption, digital ownership,
        and ways to have more control over your data.
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <b>Indie Web</b><br>
        Explore the personal, creative, and independent
        side of the web outside the major platforms.
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <b>Alternative Networks</b><br>
        Discover projects like mesh networks, federated
        services, and other ways of connecting people.
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <b>Digital Freedom</b><br>
        Talk about open standards, interoperability,
        user ownership, and a web built for everyone.
    </div>

</div>

